        </h4>
        <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300; margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;">
          <strong>Brand-Controlled Cause:</strong> If a shipment is rejected because Ghar Aangan failed to provide a required export document or because of a Ghar Aangan-controlled compliance failure, the case will be reviewed for an appropriate refund or replacement after recovery of the shipment where possible.
          <br><br>
          <strong>Destination / Customer-Side Cause:</strong> If rejection or return occurs because destination country laws prohibit the product, the importer/customer cannot complete clearance, the recipient refuses required duties or legitimate clearance charges, the address is invalid, or the customer fails to supply requested identification/documentation, any refund will be reduced by non-refundable shipping, return carriage, customs, storage, and demurrage costs.
        </p>

        <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          • Lost International Shipments
        </h4>
        <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300; margin: 0;">
          For an apparently lost international shipment, Ghar Aangan will first pursue an official investigation with the international courier and insurer. Customer remedy depends on the tracer findings, declared value, insurance coverage, and applicable law. A temporary tracking or customs delay is not automatically treated as final loss.
        </p>
